There are a few ways to terminate a C program:

1. Using the return statement:

The most common way to terminate a program in C is by using the return statement. You can use the return statement with a value, which will be returned to the calling function, or without a value, which will return 0 by default.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

2. Using the exit() function:

The exit() function is another way to terminate a program in C. It takes an integer status code as its argument, which is returned to the operating system.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    exit(0);
}
```

3. Using the return key:

If you are writing an interactive program that reads user input, the user can terminate the program by pressing the return key (or Enter key) when there is no more input to be entered.

```c

